{
  "title": "C'{ip:è} qualcuno? Non {ip:voglio} niente!",
  "translation": "Is anybody there? I don't want anything!",
  "topics": "Indefinite words, quantity words and the adverbs già, ancora, appena, quasi",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Somebody, something, nobody, nothing"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Positive",
            "Negative"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "qualcuno: somebody",
              "nessuno: nobody"
            ],
            [
              "qualcosa: something",
              "niente / nulla: nothing"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Italian keeps both negative words when the negative word comes after the verb: *Non {ip:voglio} niente. Non c'{ip:è} nessuno.* Literally, *I don't want nothing*. If *nessuno* or *niente* comes before the verb, there is no *non*: *Nessuno {ip:parla}.*",
      {
        "h": "Every, all and some"
      },
      "*Ogni* and *qualche* never change and are always followed by a singular noun, even though *qualche* means *some*: *ogni giorno, qualche volta*.",
      "*Tutto* agrees with the noun and takes the article after it. *Ogni giorno* and *tutti i giorni* mean the same.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Form",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tutto il",
              "tutto il giorno",
              "all day"
            ],
            [
              "tutta la",
              "tutta la casa",
              "the whole house"
            ],
            [
              "tutti i",
              "tutti i giorni",
              "every day"
            ],
            [
              "tutte le",
              "tutte le sere",
              "every evening"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "How much"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Word",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "troppo",
              "too, too much",
              "{ip:È} troppo caro. {ip:Mangio} troppo."
            ],
            [
              "abbastanza",
              "quite, enough",
              "{ip:È} abbastanza caro. {ip:Ho} abbastanza soldi."
            ],
            [
              "quasi",
              "almost",
              "{pp:Ho} quasi {pp:finito}."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "*Troppo* changes before a noun: *troppa gente, troppi soldi*. *Abbastanza* and *quasi* never change.",
      {
        "h": "Già, ancora and appena"
      },
      "In the [pp:passato prossimo], these words stand between the auxiliary and the participle.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Word",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "già",
              "already",
              "{pp:Ho} già {pp:mangiato}."
            ],
            [
              "non… ancora",
              "not yet",
              "Non {pp:ho} ancora {pp:mangiato}."
            ],
            [
              "appena",
              "just",
              "{pp:Sono} appena {pp:arrivato}."
            ],
            [
              "ancora",
              "still",
              "{ip:Sei} ancora qui?"
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
